# Trivy exceptions, each with a rationale and an expiry.
#
# The vendored kubectl/helm/talosctl client binaries are built by upstream with
# a Go toolchain that has not picked up these fixes yet (checked against the
# latest kubectl v1.37.1, helm v4.3.1 and talosctl v1.14.4 on 2026-10-24).
# They are CLI clients talking to operator-configured endpoints with pinned CA
# material, not network listeners; revisit when upstream rebuilds.
CVE-2026-111943 exp:2027-01-31
CVE-2026-78667 exp:2027-01-31
CVE-2026-78669 exp:2027-01-31
CVE-2026-97031 exp:2027-01-31
CVE-2026-56851 exp:2027-01-31
# hickory-resolver 0.24 O(n^2) encoding: client-only against two hard-coded
# public resolvers for DDNS discovery (see rust/deny.toml).
GHSA-5j98-2g5x-46v6 exp:2027-03-31

# nginxinc/nginx-unprivileged:1.30.6-alpine-slim ships musl 1.2.6-r2 and
# zlib 1.3.2-r0; Alpine 3.24 has the fixes (musl 1.2.6-r3, zlib 1.3.2-r1) but
# the upstream image has not been rebuilt. It serves static files only.
CVE-2026-107891 exp:2027-01-31
